From 379beb0f122c0014f7a6c26a44b9dc4852abd76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:03:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 190/192] Aurora: sun shadows shaped as in Wind Waker HD, held
 at 24 degrees, soft toward their tips, and tinted by the sky

The sun shadow map holds the sun at 24 degrees, its direction too, and thins its shadows out from there, as Wind Waker HD does.

At the Private Oasis (Cemu, the clock running, a fixed camera) HD's shadows
stopped moving between 25 and 23 degrees (17:15-17:25), stayed put, thinned
out steadily to about half by -7 degrees and were gone by -8. Below the hold
the sun is cast from where its path crossed it: held at its height alone it
kept turning, the map turned with it every frame and the shadows in the
coarser cascades crawled. Held at 2 degrees, a low cliff's shadow reached the
horizon at sunset. The moon keeps its 2 degree hold (its dawn timing was
matched with it).

Long sun shadows soften toward their tips.

A few lookups find how far the caster is along the sun's rays, and the
filter widens with it, so a long shadow's tip is soft as in Wind Waker HD.
Where none finds anything in the way the place is lit and the filter's own
lookups are skipped. The bias doesn't grow with the widening (it changes with
distance, and shadows slid along the ground as the camera neared an island),
and the shadow doesn't fade with it (where two shadows overlap the map keeps
only the caster nearer the sun, and the overlap came out lighter).
DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_SOFT and _SOFT_MAX tune it.

Two sun shadow map debug views, how surfaces face the sun and the shadow in pink.

DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_DEBUG=7 shows each surface green toward the sun, red
away from it, white edge-on, dimmed by how lit it came out; =8 the scene as it
is with the map's shadow in pink, to find shadows on what shouldn't have any.

The sun shadow map's shadow is a colour, the shade lit by the sky, as in Wind Waker HD.

Link's shadow on Windfall's dock at noon (Cemu and BlueWake, the same stage
select spawn, the HD textures) kept 0.21, 0.39 and 0.56 of the sunlit planks'
red, green and blue in HD, and 0.65 of each here. The full shadow now
multiplies the scene by a colour, 0.22, 0.41, 0.60, blended in by how shaded a
place is: the same spot measures 0.22, 0.41, 0.61. DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOWS_COLOUR
sets it (0.65,0.65,0.65 is the old grey).

The sun shadow map has three cascades, out to 20,000 units.

The fourth, out to 80,000, held only islands deep in the haze, and its coarse
texels shaded them in blocks the haze turned light blue: Windfall, sailed
toward from sea room 10, from when its model loaded until it came into the
third cascade. With three it is lit until then, and its shadows fade in at the
third's detail. It also saves drawing the casters a fourth time each frame.
DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_CASCADES=4 puts it back.

aurora_set_sun_shadow_strength sets how dark the map's shadows are, 0 to 1
(1, the default, is HD's), the moon's too: BlueWake's menu offers lighter ones
for players who find them too dark. And the slope's share of the bias far
from the camera is 20 texels (DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_SLOPE; 10 before):
Ice Ring Isle's walls, nearly edge-on to the sun, had stripes of acne where
the far bias took over, and nearer shadows, at Dragon Roost and sea room 10,
are as they were.
